  "notes": [
    "Transport: OSC over UDP to the console (host and port from the module config); every action except exec_button sends a command string to /cmd, exec_button sends /Page<n>/Key<n>. An optional input prefix from the config is prepended to the path (actions.ts:4-14).",
    "The manifest lists only GrandMA3. The module help describes control of 'grandMA3 Software' and a LUA plugin for grandMA3 onPC, but there is no separate onPC module and no statement about hardware consoles; onPC versus console coverage is not verified.",
    "Actions come in number and name pairs (for example group and group_name); the name variants are plain text inputs without useVariables. Only the command action resolves variables (useVariables).",
    "The only feedback, sequence_active, is driven by OSC messages the console sends to the module's feedback port; it reads address 14.14.1.6 (main.ts handleOSCMessage) and depends on the console-side OSC output setup.",
    "exec_button hides the 'page' number when 'current_page' is checked; the condition is isVisibleExpression '$(options:current_page)==false' in the source.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.14.1: no expressions; the isVisibleExpression above only controls visibility."
  ]
}
